\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Choosing a sign from a pair}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{At a self-opposite label an inversion can act within the negative part of the Hermitian kernel. The two members of an antiunitary pair need not have been chosen as inversion eigenvectors. Which common eigenspace carries the sign, and how much of its dimension should count?}
